      "nets": ["+3V3", "Net-(U15-Y)"],
      "observed": "R62 is listed with value '10' (ohms) in the netlist and SPICE deck.",
      "expected": "R62 should be 10kΩ, as indicated by its MPN 0603WAF1002T5E (10k) and its role as a pull-up on U15's output; R61 and R63 in the same e-stop chain are 10K.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "R62 | 10 | Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric | MotorController:TAYLOR_RESISTOR |  | LCSC=C25804, MPN= 0603WAF1002T5E, Manufacturer=UNI-ROYAL(Uniroyal Elec)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R62 +3V3 Net-_U15-Y_ 10"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A 10Ω pull-up to 3.3V on U15's output will prevent U15 from pulling the node low and may damage the buffer, breaking the e-stop chain.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U10.4", "U10.5", "U11.4", "U11.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U10 and U11 have both GND1 (logic side) and GND2 (bus side) connected to the same GND net.",
      "expected": "For isolated CAN buses as stated in the spec, GND1 and GND2 should be on separate grounds (logic ground and isolated bus ground).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "GND [High Power] : ... U10.4(GND1,power_in) U10.5(GND2,power_in) ... U11.4(GND1,power_in) U11.5(GND2,power_in) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver (`U11`/companion)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Galvanic isolation between the logic and CAN bus sides is defeated, allowing ground loops and eliminating the protective isolation.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["D30", "R60"],
      "pins": ["D30.2", "D30.4", "R60.1", "R60.2"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_OUT", "Net-(D30-K2)"],
      "observed": "D30's second LED anode (pin 4) is on ESTOP_OUT, and its cathode (pin 2) connects through R60 to ESTOP_OUT as well (R60.2 on ESTOP_OUT).",
      "expected": "The cathode resistor R60 should connect to GND, so the LED lights when ESTOP_OUT is high.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "ESTOP_OUT : D30.4(A2,input) ... R60.2(passive) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(D30-K2) : D30.2(K2,input) R60.1(passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "D30's second LED is shorted and will never illuminate, so the e-stop status indication is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: R62 is a 10Ω pull-up instead of 10kΩ, the isolated CAN transceivers have their grounds tied together, and the D30 status LED is shorted."
}

